Yury Ivanovich (23 March 1480 – 8 March 1536) ;

Yury Ivanovich (Russian: Юрий Ива́нович; 23 March 1480 – 3 August 1536) was the second surviving son of Ivan III and his wife Sophia Paleologue. Since 1519, his appanages included Dmitrovskoe knjazevstvo.
When his elder brother Vasily III ascended to the throne, Yury was 24 years old. Like his other brothers, he was forbidden to marry until Vasily could produce an heir and even then he was not allowed to marry without the ruler's permission.
